# Timer: the explore lab's ALLOCATOR loop (`/desk`), weekly Friday 10:00
# America/Los_Angeles. Successor to `pulse-elevate.timer` (rename decision
# 2026-07-26, bead explore-mqvu; transition constraints explore-b47q).
# Schedule is IDENTICAL to the timer it replaces — a rename, not a cadence change.
# It sits between the 06:00 and 12:00 dive fires so the two loops never overlap.
#
# ✅ INSTALLED 2026-07-26. All six steps of the flip completed and verified:
#   1. /desk skill + refs/pulse.md `desk` row + "Archived rows" table  ✓
#   2. pulse-elevate.timer disabled                                     ✓
#   3. stamp CARRIED ACROSS — stamp-pulse-desk.timer dated Fri 2026-07-24
#      17:00 (the old elevate run), so NO phantom catch-up tick fired.
#      This is the mechanism that matters: systemd's persistence state is
#      /var/lib|~/.local/share/systemd/timers/stamp-<unit>.timer, NOT the
#      unit file's mtime — a new unit name has no stamp, which reads as an
#      elapsed slot and fires immediately on enable.
#      (agents/infra.md "Timer-rename gotcha")                          ✓
#   4. units installed, daemon-reload, enable --now                     ✓
#   5. ~/harnessd/refs/harness-manifest.json updated (timer+ledger_row) ✓
#   6. systemd-analyze calendar verified                                ✓
#
# FIRST FIRE: Fri 2026-07-31 — /desk has never actually run. The skill was
# re-architected before that fire (explore-f7m7): the single-context design was
# rejected on review and replaced by Pass A (wide, proposes) -> Pass B (narrow,
# corpus-free, verifies + writes). See refs/lab-open-questions.md.
#
# explore-b47q: the old elevate pulse is ARCHIVED, not migrated. Its ledger rows
# stay under `"row":"elevate"` as history; `desk` starts a FRESH row.
[Unit]
Description=Pulse timer: weekly /desk pass (explore lab resourcing memo)

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Fri *-*-* 10:00:00 America/Los_Angeles
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
